[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says the reports about dates are one issue with one fix queued. Read
by cause instead of by subject line, the same reports hold three problems. The parser fix
closes only the first one.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket. Do not close the others when the parser
fix ships.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

Counted once per report id: the ticket export repeats some reports across its pages. A problem
is placed by the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not by intake's tag, which
guesses from the reporter's browser and is wrong in both directions.

## The problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads every date month first.** Every tenant on file writes the
day first. A date with both parts at 12 or below comes out with day and month swapped
("7 April went out on 4 July"); every tenant and every channel is affected. This is the fix
#4471 has queued.

**`hint` — booking-v3's form tells people to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`, so people type month first, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day
first. Only reports through the form at tenants on booking-v3 (Alder Physio, Copper Studio,
Pale Harbour). The symptom is the same swap, so subject lines merge it into #4471, but the
parser fix does not touch it: the hint is wrong, the parser is not involved.

**`one-day-move` — the date moves by one day, not a swap.** The desk already noted these
(`desk-notes.json`): "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday.", "Every
booking in June is one day off", an invite that arrived before the booking was made. A day
boundary between time zones, not day/month order. Neither the parser fix nor the hint fix
touches it.

## Why they ended up in one ticket

Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) puts every
"wrong date" report in one place, whatever the cause. The table on #4471 already shows the
split: it marks `hint` as "not this ticket — no ticket of its own" and footnotes the one-day
moves under `parser`. Nobody filed them.

## What the desk does now

1. Keep #4471 for `parser` only.
2. Route new form reports from booking-v3 tenants to the `hint` ticket.
3. Route reports where the date moved by one day (no swap) to the `one-day-move` ticket.

The counts above are built from the export at render time. The tickets carry the count from
the export they were filed from; when the desk merges more reports, rebuild this page and
update the tickets from it.

